course: dictionary
lesson: 2842
title: The busy word do
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Do is a small word with many jobs. Sometimes it is an action word, as in «do your homework», which means carry out a task. Sometimes it is a helper that works with another verb to make a question or a «not» sentence.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Inside the Arctic and Antarctic Circles, there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set.» Does is the helper here. It works with not and set to say the Sun does not go down that day. Helpers like do make sentences work.
explain: Do can also stand in for a verb that has already been said. Read this: «Who ate the last biscuit?» «I did.» Did means I ate it, so you do not need to repeat the whole action. Context tells you which verb do stands for.
explain: Do has casual meanings too. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a do is a party, so a birthday do is a birthday party. «Done in» means very tired. Context tells you which meaning to choose, so check the words around it.
fact: Do is a verb: it means to carry out an action, as in «do the dishes».
fact: As a helper, do makes questions and «not» sentences: «Do you like cats?» and «I don't know».
fact: Does and did are forms of the same helper: «Does Ben have any cards?» and «Did you see it?»
fact: Do can stand in for an earlier verb: «Who ate it?» «I did.»
fact: «That will do» means that is enough, and «done in» means very tired.
exercise: «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them.» What job does did do in this sentence? | Meaning a party | Standing for a verb already said | Meaning hurt | *Helping make a «not» sentence
exercise: Dad says, «That will do, we have enough cake.» What does will do mean here? | That will hurt you | *That is enough | That will be a party | That is a big job
exercise: Find and copy the word that stands for a verb already said: «Who ate the last biscuit?» «I did.» | I | last | ate | *did
test: In «Real otters do not chase May-flies», what job does do have? | Meaning a party | Meaning very tired | *Helping make a «not» sentence | Standing for an earlier verb
test: Ella says, «I was done in after the long walk.» What does done in mean? | Having a party | Caught by the police | Fastened up | *Very tired
exam: In an exam, the words «perform» and «carry out» mean the same as which everyday word? | Dance | *Do | Dog | Dinner
